    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "polynomial may not achieve the maximum allowable number of roots given by the Fundamental Theorem of Algebra, but this bound is sharp, in the sense that given a natural number n there exist a polynomial of degree n which has exactly n zeros counting multiplicities."
  }, {
    "type" : "list",
